{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1192509-other-talent-gift-ideas","id":1192509,"title":"Other Talent Gift Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-06T21:15:49-08:00","id":1192509,"title":"Other Talent Gift Ideas","content":"I'm thinking about source media tropes that would be appropriate as additional Talent Gifts.<br /> <br /> - False Identity: inspired by Leverage and Person of Interest, the incredible ability to weave up on the fly new identities that withstand background investigations, and that the character can perform flawlessly, seems appropriate for Talents. I'm thinking it has Technology and Larceny ratings needed, and can be taken as either associated Gift; at least in modern or future settings with information network technology. If you're in a setting without the internet, it's straight Larceny, cooking up the forged documents and contacts who will vouch for you on the fly.<br /> <br /> - Knock unconscious: a Medicine or Close Combat Gift that via a strong enough hit (so one that would do significant damage) you instead rule it does no lasting damage but perfectly knocks the subject out without other harm or risk. In a setting with mind control effects, this might also be able to snap a subject out of it.<br /> <br /> - Possibly another Knack that allows you to rule your OWN CHARACTER is knocked out for the rest of the scene rather than taking real damage; minions and minor enemies are compelled to ignore you after that point if you weren't their specific goal, more significant opponents can resist that however (Giles had this Gift on Buffy)<br /> <br /> <br /> Any thoughts on these? Ideas of your own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T21:30:19-08:00","id":1192958,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Another idea: I need to review the mechanics to see how defense against surprise attacks normally work, but basically provided the character is unaware of the attack, they player can spend Inspiration to use their normal or even enhanced defense, and this plays out as a completely lucky coincidence. Like the character bending over to pick something up right as a sniper fires.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Or is that something that seems like it would be covered by normal Dramatic Editing?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T21:52:11-08:00","id":1192964,"title":"","content":"Another idea: traps don't work the way they're supposed to - giving you an opportunity to disarm them even after they've been triggered. See the trope of landmines not going off after they've been stepped on so long as the person stays put.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:14:00-08:00","id":1193378,"title":"","content":"Would counter-hacking with vigorous typing to, taking control of your opponents system in their attempt to hack you be worthy of a Gift, or is that more of a Skill Trick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:38:21-08:00","id":1193443,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Another possibility: the ability for someone to impossibly cross-reference databases using the most esoteric of parameters to narrow down information creating an instant suspect/candidate/location/whatever list.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As seen in: almost every episode of Criminal Minds</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T23:20:44-08:00","id":1193449,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Wait.... how is Death Defiance a purchasable Gift, when that exact effect is listed with the same price (3 Inspiration) on page 174, as an application of Dramatic Editing that all Talents are capable of without any Attribute prerequisite or Gift purchase?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}